# Finite-volume orientation notes

These notes summarize the public finite-volume context needed to start reading
the supplied source snapshot.

- PyBaMM builds symbolic PDE models and discretises them by the method of
  lines.
- In one-dimensional finite-volume methods, scalar unknowns are commonly stored
  at cell centers, while flux-like quantities live on cell edges.
- Boundary values influence the edge-level flux balance through the package's
  finite-volume boundary representation.
- Advection-dominated transport requires a direction-aware edge state before
  applying the finite-volume divergence.

The source snapshot and official API page contain the package-specific details.
The public reproduction is intended as a deterministic workbench, not as a
complete correctness oracle.
